  "description": "The autism DSM-ADI-R (ADAR) ontology extends an ontology by Tu et al. with additional SWRL rules to infer phenotypes from ADI-R items.\r\nIt includes OWL class definitions representing DSM IV diagnostic criteria for autistic disorder and ASD criteria for Autism Spectrum Disorder\r\nOWL Reasoners can thus infer autism-related phenotypes from ADI-R questionnaire results \r\n\r\nTu SW, Tennakoon L, Connor MO, Das A. Using an Integrated Ontology and Information Model for Querying and Reasoning about Phenotypes : The Case of Autism. AMIA Annu Symp Proc 2008;727–31\r\n",
